.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    Let an employee acknowledge the true job description they are held to, and let anyone who can open the manager job description see the current wording and every past signature.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  %p.mb-3
    A signature freezes this page. Later edits to assignments, energy, milestones, or seat labels do not change a signature that was already made. Signing is something the employee does. A manager can read signatures, not create one for somebody else.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 What you see
  %ul.mb-3
    %li A green banner means a signature already covers the latest position change or finalized position check-in. A warning banner means a signature is still needed.
    %li Past signatures appear at the top. Each one links to the wording that was stored at that time.
    %li Seat labels always appear at the top and bottom. If there is no seat, each field says to correct it in Seat Management for this person.
    %li The current job description lists active assignments with their energy percentage.
    %li A required assignment with no active tenure shows at 0%, with a warning that they need to be taking on that assignment.
    %li Assignment ability lines match the print True JD. A Required Abilities section lists each ability, its description, and each milestone needed, including which Assignments require at least that milestone.
    %li The employee signs by typing the full name on their account. One signature is enough even if a check-in and a position change both happened recently.
